#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060569} :activity/id #uuid "1f56b8ef-868f-57e2-ae40-b8e705105170" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050360 :topic/id #uuid "4264930a-5f20-54f0-ad2a-c3ad45c03658" :topic/math-academy-id 250} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060569 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060983 :tutorial/content "A **conditional statement** (or **implication**) is a mathematical statement that takes the form\n\n$\\qquad$ *$P$ implies $Q,$*\n\nor equivalently,\n\n$\\qquad$ *if $P,$ then $Q.$*\n\nSymbolically, it can be written as $P \\Rightarrow Q,$ where $P$ is called the **antecedent** (or **hypothesis**) and $Q$ is called the **consequent** (or **conclusion**).\n\nThe truth table for $P \\Rightarrow Q$ is shown below.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\, P \\Rightarrow Q \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n\nIntuitively, an implication can be viewed as a \"promise\" that whenever $P$ is true, $Q$ is also true. The implication is true unless the promise is broken, i.e., $P$ is true, and $Q$ is false.\n\nWe'll discuss the intuition behind implications in more detail later in the lesson." :tutorial/id #uuid "a6598728-1780-50b5-af45-ace426318bc6" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7977 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "62e05d8d-2ee3-5cd5-8592-01e6eef66d71" :step/math-academy-id 154035 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060570}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060570 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059699 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059408 :question/id #uuid "8831a019-f252-5678-9855-6c0f1da89f77" :question/math-academy-id "e-12706"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "df9791a3-465d-57e4-8f2e-40fb9fb18d70" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060135} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060136} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376268} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376274} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376292} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376302}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Truth Values of Implications"} :step/id #uuid "89220a35-670a-5c3b-9161-aa844a949880" :step/math-academy-id 154036 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060571}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060571 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059700 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059407 :question/id #uuid "0b97d670-694b-52e5-aa55-1224985f83a8" :question/math-academy-id "e-12705"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e1c01fd-dea0-5761-9499-d622a34fea3e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050777}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060137} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060151} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060152} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376388} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376401} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390071} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390113} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406951}] :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Truth Table With Compound Statements"} :step/id #uuid "cb82b9e6-f25a-5610-8374-2261c53cde3b" :step/math-academy-id 154039 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060572}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060572 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060994 :tutorial/content "Let's recall the truth table for $P\\Rightarrow Q.$\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\, P \\Rightarrow Q \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n\nWe consider a concrete example to build further intuition behind the truth values in this table.\n\nSuppose your teacher promises that *if* you score at least $90$ on the exam, *then* you will receive an A. In other words, the teacher has promised that a score of at least $90$ on the exam implies that you will receive an A: $$\\textrm{Score at least 90} \\: \\Rightarrow \\: \\textrm{Receive an A}$$\n\nNow, the teacher may or may not be lying. The implication is true if the teacher tells the truth and false if the teacher lies.\n\nThe following four situations are possible:\n\n1. You score $90$ and receive an A. In this case, the teacher has told the truth. They have kept the promise. $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n2. You score $90$ and do *not* receive an A. In this case, the teacher has lied. They have broken the promise. $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n3. You do *not* score $90,$ yet you receive an A. In this case, the teacher has told the truth! The promise does not apply because you did not score at least $90.$ $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n4. You do *not* score $90$ and do *not* receive an A. Again, the teacher has told the truth. The promise does not apply because you did not score at least $90.$ $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\nEach of these situations corresponds to a row in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\textrm{At least 90}$ | $\\textrm{Receive an A}$ | $\\textrm{Score at least 90} \\Rightarrow \\textrm{Receive an A}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{black} \\textrm T$ |" :tutorial/id #uuid "6943ab9c-bf27-5dbb-9871-a5647b7d3b74" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8292 :tutorial/title "Intuition Behind the Implication Truth Table"} :step/id #uuid "4b3b0e3b-bca5-585d-999e-a2ea88c36b2b" :step/math-academy-id 154043 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060573}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060573 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059701 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059406 :question/id #uuid "13e5834d-4d70-5893-a4bf-9927000d522d" :question/math-academy-id "e-12704"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64a3922f-7e74-562f-9bb9-c4a41e912ce7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060411} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060417} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375631} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375687} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377865} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377872} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377879} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406949} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406950}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Conditional Statements"} :step/id #uuid "ea087540-046f-51b4-a818-16971088b6d6" :step/math-academy-id 154044}] :activity/title "Conditional Statements" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059928}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046673} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406953} :activity/id #uuid "e3bb9df3-04b6-5d77-8062-3bd56ac21bf2" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050360 :topic/id #uuid "4264930a-5f20-54f0-ad2a-c3ad45c03658" :topic/math-academy-id 250} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406952 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406949 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a11b4773-38d5-5c0c-9e9c-3e0b4ecae818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453132} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab874b5-03d7-53c3-b6db-a652d9c156a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453133}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453132} :answer-field/id #uuid "26f8e36a-498b-5385-816f-6d262d6c4893" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454316} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96553132-07aa-5dd8-a9d9-80d5ba1e0f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453134} {:answer/id #uuid "f12b50d9-97e8-547c-ae5c-e9776f0678cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453135}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453135} :answer-field/id #uuid "cae81137-1867-50f5-a1a9-e15ecfd57220" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "923f9c82-2491-5942-a700-0059eb11d931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453136} {:answer/id #uuid "bca078d7-e26d-5c8c-ac29-1d2b30f25905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453137}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453137} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8ffb718-a2da-578a-a502-45fd1b77e827" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "55e540af-11e2-5ec3-9b47-ab0da3ac740e" :question/math-academy-id "q-103558" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** **If** $12$ is divisible by $3$, **then** $9$ is divisible by $4.$\n- **II.** **If** $5$ is divisible by $2$, **then** $10$ is divisible by $5.$\n- **III.** **If** $9$ is divisible by $5$, **then** $6$ is divisible by $3.$" :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is false. The antecedent \"$12$ is divisible by $3$\" is true, and the consequent \"$9$ is divisible by $4$\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. The antecedent \"$5$ is divisible by $2$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent \"$9$ is divisible by $5$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "52b92551-8e29-55f1-ae0e-36ee601e078e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406954}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406953 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406950 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20959140-93b8-5a47-a197-da32ff4810aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454066} {:answer/id #uuid "9379cea3-738f-5b45-9ffb-a0d389c84fcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454067}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186454067} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecc3054a-806e-55e3-a67b-9d3aafb6ab0e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454783} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "862f1c15-7d4f-5155-be39-3424fe47a6a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454068} {:answer/id #uuid "e30f18bc-42c2-57a7-8e53-faed108c78b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454069}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186454068} :answer-field/id #uuid "6338d248-c558-59d6-b0d2-c36e277fc0ef" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454784} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ff828bb-30f0-59e3-937e-d221fd6fafb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454070} {:answer/id #uuid "5d13fad8-f3e6-549c-954e-a199b234815c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454071}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186454071} :answer-field/id #uuid "693882b2-096a-516e-95d6-0393826e4576" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454785}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "806aafe6-aa9d-53f3-a7d9-19809d388a29" :question/math-academy-id "q-82092" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** **If** $7$ is an even number, **then** $6$ is an odd number.\n- **II.** **If** $6$ is an even number, **then** $7$ is an even number.\n- **III.** **If** $6$ is an even number, **then** $7$ is an odd number." :question/worked-solution "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true. The antecedent \"$7$ is an even number\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The antecedent \"$6$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$7$ is an even number\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. The antecedent \"$6$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$7$ is an odd number\" is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "c4e3aeea-5769-5fb5-81bc-48e1231cf682" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406952}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406954 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406951 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a334099-1f7f-5c0b-aead-371217a694de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406935} {:answer/id #uuid "a2888028-3901-5c34-ae8a-4a28ac3aca86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406938}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406938} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aee77f4-9be5-5c3a-80a1-10941ff43d8b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406944} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e14bb50-b52f-54ce-95fb-59ff76aadc0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406927} {:answer/id #uuid "f722b6c6-65d9-5629-96ce-1fb6fc2acbcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406942}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406942} :answer-field/id #uuid "5567147c-6f0e-52d8-9449-dc159b1a7899" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406945} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6931d52b-ab40-549d-8508-bab0ac42c5ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406932} {:answer/id #uuid "74e8728a-9112-5092-beaa-752dfc425e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406934}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406932} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a198ffa-6bcf-5c46-8bb4-49b21b82a7a8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406946} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d6a50a3-bb24-530f-a62b-129c6bdb591b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406930} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a03093-15bd-5e22-b3ec-be4928468ac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406940}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186406930} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4032492-1493-553b-bc31-fe628a9c1050" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e0bd03cd-0c48-596c-b039-0f9c85a18c3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-182663" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,P⇒(¬P∨¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, we add columns for $¬P,$ $¬Q$ and $¬P∨¬Q:$\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nNow, we add a column for $P⇒(¬P∨¬Q).$ This statement is true unless $P$ is true and $¬P∨¬Q$ is false. \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨¬Q\\,$ | $\\,P⇒(¬P∨¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |"} :step/id #uuid "ebbb7ea7-a0d0-5fb6-9455-eb7f19b0c1b3"}] :activity/title "Conditional Statements" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186406924}]}
